<dtml-var manage_page_header>
<dtml-var manage_tabs>
<h1>README</h1>
<p>To add local events from ZCataloged items in your RDFCalendar you need to
add a Stript (Python) with an id in this form: <strong>local_</strong>script</p>
<p>The script is required to return a list of dictionaries which is then used to
display the calendar. Also you must provide these arguments to the Script: year=None, month=None, day=None</p>
<p>Here is an example:</p>
<p>Script (Python) <strong>local_events</strong>:</p>
<p>
    <pre>
    return context.rdf_cataloged_items('Event', year=year, month=month, day=day)
    </pre>
</p>
<p>This returns a list of dictionaries containing the data of the Naaya Events
items. Start and end dates, id, title, description, etc.</p>
<hr />
<p>If some other content type is needed then some tweaking is required by providing
a relation dictionary as rdf_cataloged_items argument.</p>
<p>For example:</p>
<p>Script (Python) <strong>local_custom_events</strong>:</p>
<p>
    <pre>
    relations = {
        'startdate': 'start_date'
    }
    return context.rdf_cataloged_items('Custom Event', relations, year=year, month=month, day=day)
    </pre>
</p>
<p>
This matches startdate field that is required in the RDFCalendar with start_date
attribute that can be found in Naaya Custom Event. You can customize all the fields like this.
</p>
<p>Here is the list of available keys:</p>
<p>'author', 'creator', 'dc_coverage', 'dc_description', 'dc_format',
'dc_identifier', 'dc_source', 'dc_type', 'enddate', 'id', 'language',
'link', 'location', 'link', 'location', 'organizer', 'publisher',
'rdfsubject', 'rights', 'startdate', 'subtitle', 'summary', 'title',
'type'</p>
